<item>
            <title>[LU-20803] P3: Prefix-hole object write</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20803</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Summary&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Summary&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open OBJECT-scope direct pwrite for the prefix hole only, so the next component&apos;s object can be filled in place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Description&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A PFL object&apos;s prefix hole &lt;tt&gt;[0, obj(e_start))&lt;/tt&gt; does not contribute to the parent &lt;tt&gt;i_size&lt;/tt&gt;, and that component&apos;s file-offset path cannot reach it. &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13612&quot; title=&quot;efficient DoM-&amp;gt;OST component migration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-13612&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13612&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; needs those bytes: copy the DoM / previous component into the next object&apos;s prefix hole and leave that object in place. Whole-file DoM&#8594;OST migration (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10177&quot; title=&quot;DoM: manual migration MDT-OST&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-10177&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10177&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-11421&quot; title=&quot;DoM: manual migration OST-MDT, MDT-MDT&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-11421&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-11421&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) already covers the product goal, at the cost of rewriting the file. P2 opened &lt;tt&gt;OBJECT&lt;/tt&gt; for &lt;tt&gt;pread&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;lseek&lt;/tt&gt; only; &lt;tt&gt;pwrite&lt;/tt&gt; is still &lt;tt&gt;-EOPNOTSUPP&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Extend that same entry path &#8212; one sub-I/O, identity mapping, &lt;tt&gt;ios_fid&lt;/tt&gt; as the only identity &#8212; to direct &lt;tt&gt;pwrite&lt;/tt&gt;, including the object&apos;s data-version update and &lt;tt&gt;fsync&lt;/tt&gt;. File-offset helpers stay unchanged. In LOV, the OBJECT iterator range-checks the write and still does not walk components. In VVP, the write start must not apply an object offset to the parent inode size.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Object-offset write ranges:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;[0, obj(e_start))&lt;/tt&gt;: accepted. This is the prefix hole.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;[obj(e_start), obj(e_end))&lt;/tt&gt;: rejected. The visible range stays file offset + &lt;tt&gt;STRIPE&lt;/tt&gt; (P1b).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;[obj(e_end), &#8734;)&lt;/tt&gt;: &lt;tt&gt;-EINVAL&lt;/tt&gt;. Nothing consumes this range.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Prefix bytes map below &lt;tt&gt;e_start&lt;/tt&gt;, so the existing composite size merge does not raise &lt;tt&gt;i_size&lt;/tt&gt;. The OBJECT write path must not update it either.&#160; &lt;tt&gt;stat&lt;/tt&gt; stays unchanged; the object size and quota do change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is not a designated resync:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Do not set &lt;tt&gt;LU_LAYOUT_RESYNC&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Non-FLR does not send &lt;tt&gt;OBD_MD_LAYOUT_VERSION&lt;/tt&gt; to the OST, so &lt;tt&gt;filter_fid.ff_layout_version&lt;/tt&gt; stays 0.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;FLR does not set the RESYNC bit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;A mutating op requires a non-zero &lt;tt&gt;ios_layout_version&lt;/tt&gt;. A mismatch with &lt;tt&gt;lsm_layout_gen&lt;/tt&gt; returns &lt;tt&gt;-ESTALE&lt;/tt&gt;. The UAPI header documents the caller contract: &lt;tt&gt;LL_LEASE_WRLCK&lt;/tt&gt;, a non-zero FID, and a non-zero layout version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Acceptance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Prefix-hole write: &lt;tt&gt;stat&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;i_size&lt;/tt&gt; unchanged; object size and quota change.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Visible-range write, and a write past &lt;tt&gt;obj(e_end)&lt;/tt&gt;, return &lt;tt&gt;-EINVAL&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Layout change returns &lt;tt&gt;-ESTALE&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Non-FLR: OST &lt;tt&gt;filter_fid.ff_layout_version&lt;/tt&gt; stays 0. FLR: no RESYNC bit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
